searchData={"items":[{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir","doc":"A Node-RED-style flow engine for Home Assistant, in Elixir.\n\nFlows are plain `.ex` files in `flows/`; the app connects to Home Assistant\nover its WebSocket API and runs the flows as an OTP supervision tree.","ref":"HomeElixir.html"},{"type":"module","title":"The big picture - HomeElixir","doc":"| Module | Role |\n|--------|------|\n| `HomeElixir.Flow` | The `use HomeElixir.Flow` macro — declare nodes + wires in a flow module |\n| `HomeElixir.FlowStore` | Flow lifecycle: `list`, `load`, `unload`, `reload`, `click`, `check` |\n| `HomeElixir.Registry` | The supervised node tree that backs the loaded flows |\n| `HomeElixir.Node` | The node behaviour (`handle/2`, optional `init/1`, `trigger/2`) |\n| `HomeElixir.Nodes` | Built-in nodes: `Inject`, `Function`, `Service`, `StateChanged`, `Device`, ... |\n| `HomeElixir.HA` | The shared Home Assistant WebSocket client |\n| `HomeElixir.Msg` | The message that flows along the wires |\n| `HomeElixir.Dep` | Install a Hex dependency at runtime (Livebook-style) |","ref":"HomeElixir.html#module-the-big-picture"},{"type":"module","title":"Quickstart - HomeElixir","doc":"Write a flow module, then load it from the web UI or `flows/`:\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule HomeElixir.Flows.Kitchen do\n  use HomeElixir.Flow\n\n  def shout(m), do: %{m | payload: m.payload |> to_string() |> String.upcase()}\n\n  node(\"in\",  HomeElixir.Nodes.Inject,   ui: %{type: \"button\", label: \"Go\"})\n  node(\"cap\", HomeElixir.Nodes.Function, fun: &__MODULE__.shout/1)\n  node(\"out\", HomeElixir.Nodes.Logger)\n  wire(\"in\", \"cap\")\n  wire(\"cap\", \"out\")\nend\n```\n\nThe **Guide** (listed under *Extras*) covers writing flows, handler flows,\nweb controls, and the dev shell. The in-app **Documentation** page renders the\nsame guide; this site is the full module reference.","ref":"HomeElixir.html#module-quickstart"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.Registry","doc":"Loads and unloads flows and tracks which are running.\n\nA *flow* is an Elixir module using `HomeElixir.Flow`. Loading it spawns a\nsupervised process per node and wires them together; unloading tears it down.","ref":"HomeElixir.Registry.html"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Registry.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"HomeElixir.Registry.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Registry.list/0","doc":"All currently loaded flow modules.","ref":"HomeElixir.Registry.html#list/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Registry.load/1","doc":"Load a flow module. Returns `{:ok, pid}` or `{:error, reason}`.","ref":"HomeElixir.Registry.html#load/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Registry.loaded?/1","doc":"Whether a flow module is loaded.","ref":"HomeElixir.Registry.html#loaded?/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Registry.node_state/2","doc":"Read a node's internal state (for tests / debug).","ref":"HomeElixir.Registry.html#node_state/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Registry.send_msg/3","doc":"Cast a message into a node of a loaded flow.","ref":"HomeElixir.Registry.html#send_msg/3"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Registry.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Registry.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Registry.ui_elements/0","doc":"UI elements declared by loaded flows. Collects nodes whose config has a\n`ui:` map and returns `[%{module, node_id, ui}]`.","ref":"HomeElixir.Registry.html#ui_elements/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Registry.unload/1","doc":"Unload a flow module (stops all its nodes).","ref":"HomeElixir.Registry.html#unload/1"},{"type":"task","title":"mix docs.inject_base","doc":"Injects a client-side ` ` into each\n`priv/static/docs/*.html` right after ` `.\n\nThe ExDoc site is a static sub-site. Its links are relative, so they only\nresolve correctly when the browser's URL already carries the sub-path. Setting\nan explicit ` ` anchored at the site's own root makes it work under any\nreverse-proxy / HA-ingress prefix (the prefix is computed in the browser, since\nbehind HA ingress the supervisor only reveals it client-side).","ref":"Mix.Tasks.Docs.InjectBase.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Mix.Tasks.Docs.InjectBase.run/1","doc":"","ref":"Mix.Tasks.Docs.InjectBase.html#run/1"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.Flow","doc":"Declare a flow as an Elixir module.\n\n   defmodule Flows.Kitchen do\n     use HomeElixir.Flow\n\n     def exclaim(m), do: %{m | payload: m.payload <> \"!\"}\n\n     node(\"in\",  HomeElixir.Nodes.Inject, payload: \"hi\")\n     node(\"f\",   HomeElixir.Nodes.Function, fun: &__MODULE__.exclaim/1)\n     node(\"out\", HomeElixir.Nodes.Sink)\n     wire(\"in\", \"f\")\n     wire(\"f\", \"out\")\n   end\n\n`__flow__` returns the declared nodes and wires; `HomeElixir.Registry` turns\nthat into a supervised process tree. Node config must be data (or a remote\nfunction like `&Mod.fun/1`); transforms are plain functions on the flow.\n\nA flow may also define `setup/0`. It runs once when the flow is loaded,\nbefore any node starts — use it to install external deps at load time\n(Livebook-style), without editing `mix.exs`:\n\n   def setup, do: HomeElixir.Dep.install([{:timex, \"~> 3.7\"}])\n\nA flow may instead define `handle/1` (a \"handler flow\"). It is wired to a\nHome Assistant `state_changed` source automatically. Its return value is\nforwarded to the nodes wired after `__he_handle__` — so state-changing\nclauses return a value (the FlowState op's result does) to wake display\nnodes, and unmatched input falls through the catch-all, which returns nil\nand is dropped:\n\n   defmodule Flows.DoorWatch do\n     use HomeElixir.Flow\n     def handle(%{topic: \"sensor.front_door\", payload: \"open\"}) do\n       ... # do work\n     end\n   end\n\nThe catch-all clause is added for you; write only the clauses you need.\n\nFlows may also persist state between runs via `HomeElixir.FlowState` (Mnesia;\nsurvives reloads and restarts). The flow's own module is the implicit key, so\nflows can't collide:\n\n    def handle(%{topic: \"sensor.front_door\", payload: \"open\"}),\n      do: HomeElixir.FlowState.update(:count, &(&1 + 1), 0)","ref":"HomeElixir.Flow.html"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState","doc":"Persistent per-flow state, namespaced by the calling flow's module.\n\nCall these from a flow's `handle/1`, a node transform, or `setup/0` — no module\nargument needed. The current flow is taken from the ambient context (the node\nprocess running the code), so two flows using the same key can't stomp on each\nother's state:\n\n     HomeElixir.FlowState.update(:count, &(&1 + 1))\n     HomeElixir.FlowState.get(:last_entity)\n     HomeElixir.FlowState.delete(:last_entity)\n\n  Backed by a Mnesia table — on disk by default (survives restarts; needs the\n  app to run as a named node), in-memory when `:flow_state_disc` is false or\n  the node is nonode@nohost — so state survives flow reloads and restarts.\n  Started by `HomeElixir.Application`.\n\nFrom outside a node (tests, scripts), target a flow explicitly with `as/2`:\n\n    HomeElixir.FlowState.as(MyFlow, fn -> HomeElixir.FlowState.get(:count) end)","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.all_flow_owners/0","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#all_flow_owners/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.all_last_triggered/0","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#all_last_triggered/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.archive/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#archive/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.archived_names/0","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#archived_names/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.as/2","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#as/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.assign_owner_if_new/2","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#assign_owner_if_new/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.clear_flow_owner/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#clear_flow_owner/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.current_flow/0","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#current_flow/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.delete/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#delete/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.ever_loaded_names/0","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#ever_loaded_names/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.flow_owner/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#flow_owner/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.forget_flow/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#forget_flow/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.forget_triggered/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#forget_triggered/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.get/2","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#get/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.is_archived?/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#is_archived?/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.last_triggered/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#last_triggered/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.loaded_checksums/0","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#loaded_checksums/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.loaded_names/0","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#loaded_names/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.loaded_source/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#loaded_source/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.owned_flow_names/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#owned_flow_names/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.public_owner/0","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#public_owner/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.put/2","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#put/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.record_load/3","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#record_load/3"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.record_triggered/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#record_triggered/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.save_loaded_names/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#save_loaded_names/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.set_flow/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#set_flow/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.set_flow_owner/2","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#set_flow_owner/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.start/0","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#start/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.stop/0","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#stop/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.unarchive/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#unarchive/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowState.update/3","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowState.html#update/3"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.FlowStore","doc":"Discovers flow `.ex` files and loads/unloads them at runtime.\n\nFlow files live in a directory (default `flows/`, overridable via the\n`:home_elixir, :flows_dir` config). Each file defines one flow module;\n`load/1` compiles the file if needed and starts it via `HomeElixir.Registry`,\n`unload/1` stops it.\n\nThe module atom for each file is taken from the compiler's result and cached,\nsince `String.to_atom/1` does not reliably yield a matching atom in all VMs.","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.html"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.archive/1","doc":"Archive a flow: force-unload it and hide it from the flow list.","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.html#archive/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.check/1","doc":"Compile a source string and report the result, without loading it into the\nflow set. Runs in this GenServer (a stable process), not the request process.","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.html#check/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.click/3","doc":"Inject a message into a node of a loaded flow (used by web controls).","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.html#click/3"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.clone/1","doc":"Clone a flow into a sibling file/module with a `Clone` suffix. Returns `{:ok, new_name}`.","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.html#clone/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.delete/1","doc":"Delete a flow: unload it, remove its file, and drop its saved state.","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.html#delete/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.flow_ui/1","doc":"UI elements for one flow (loaded or not), with live `value` when loaded.","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.html#flow_ui/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.list/0","doc":"All flow files in the flows dir, each with its name, path, module, and loaded state.","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.html#list/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.load/1","doc":"Compile a flow from disk and start it (runs its `setup/0`, if any).","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.html#load/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.loaded?/1","doc":"Whether a flow is currently loaded (without compiling it).","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.html#loaded?/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.loaded_source/1","doc":"The source at the flow's last successful load (for editor revert); `:error` if never loaded.","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.html#loaded_source/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.reload/1","doc":"Recompile a flow from disk and restart it (or load it if not running).","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.html#reload/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.reload_all/0","doc":"Reload every currently-loaded flow from disk.","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.html#reload_all/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.rename/2","doc":"Rename a flow after the editor changed its module name. The new file has\nalready been written by the caller; this unloads the old flow (if running),\nremoves the old file, and carries the old flow's ownership to the new name.","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.html#rename/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.restore/0","doc":"Load the flows that were loaded last run (persisted in the Mnesia flow-state\nDB). On the very first run (nothing saved yet) this imports the legacy\n`flows/.loaded` file if present, else loads every flow file, establishing the\nset. Flows that fail to load are logged and skipped.","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.html#restore/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.ui/0","doc":"UI elements declared by loaded flows (name-keyed, for the web UI).","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.html#ui/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.unarchive/1","doc":"Restore an archived flow back to the flow list (does not load it).","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.html#unarchive/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.unload/1","doc":"Stop a loaded flow.","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowStore.html#unload/1"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.FlowsHA","doc":"Exposes every flow as a switch in a single \"Flows\" device in Home Assistant,\nvia the Node-RED Companion integration. Each switch's state is the flow's\nloaded state; toggling it in HA loads/unloads the flow.\n\nOn every sync (at boot, after any create/delete/archive/restore, and on a\ntimer) the Flows device is reconciled against the live flow set: HA entities\nwith no matching non-archived flow are removed, and switches for current flows\nare (re)discovered. The device's current switches are read from HA's REST\n`/api/states` (the reliable source — the WS `get_states` list does not return\nthese entities), so orphaned entities are cleaned up even if they predate this\nprocess's memory of them.\n\nA no-op when HA is not configured.","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowsHA.html"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowsHA.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowsHA.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowsHA.flow_switch_ids/1","doc":"Pure: the Flows-device switch node_ids present in a `/api/states` list. HA names\nthem `switch.flows_ `, so the node_id is the suffix after that prefix;\nany other entity (other devices, other domains) is ignored.","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowsHA.html#flow_switch_ids/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowsHA.node_id/1","doc":"The switch node_id for a flow name (`/` → `_`, downcased).","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowsHA.html#node_id/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.FlowsHA.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.FlowsHA.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.Msg","doc":"A message flowing through a flow, Node-RED-style. `payload` is the primary\nvalue; `topic` and `data` carry metadata; extra fields live in `data`.","ref":"HomeElixir.Msg.html"},{"type":"type","title":"HomeElixir.Msg.t/0","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Msg.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Msg.new/2","doc":"Build a message: `Msg.new(\"hi\", topic: \"x\")`.","ref":"HomeElixir.Msg.html#new/2"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"HomeElixir.Node","doc":"Behaviour for flow nodes.\n\n`handle/2` turns one incoming message into a list of output messages; the\nengine currently forwards output index 0 only (multi-output is a later add).\n`init/1` is optional — a node that does not define it starts with state `nil`.\n\n`trigger/2` is optional for source/in nodes: it is called with an external\nevent (e.g. `{:ha_event, ref, event}`) so the node can emit messages without\nan input.","ref":"HomeElixir.Node.html"},{"type":"type","title":"HomeElixir.Node.msg/0","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Node.html#t:msg/0"},{"type":"type","title":"HomeElixir.Node.outputs/0","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Node.html#t:outputs/0"},{"type":"type","title":"HomeElixir.Node.state/0","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Node.html#t:state/0"},{"type":"callback","title":"HomeElixir.Node.handle/2","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Node.html#c:handle/2"},{"type":"callback","title":"HomeElixir.Node.init/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Node.html#c:init/1"},{"type":"callback","title":"HomeElixir.Node.trigger/2","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Node.html#c:trigger/2"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.Nodes.Device","doc":"Presents a device (entity) to Home Assistant via the Node-RED integration and\nowns its state bidirectionally.\n\nOn load it registers the device with HA (`nodered/discovery`) and keeps a\nchannel on that message id. When the entity is toggled in the HA frontend, HA\npushes a frame back on that id; this node echoes the state back so the entity\nsticks, then emits it into the flow (source). When a message arrives (e.g. from\na web button), it sets the entity's state via `nodered/entity` (sink). The node\nalso tracks its current state, so a `ui: %{type: \"state\"}` element can display it.\n\nConfig:\n  * `server_id`, `node_id` — identify the device (required, unique per device)\n  * `component` — `\"switch\"` (also `sensor`/`button`/`binary_sensor`), default `\"switch\"`\n  * `config` — entity display: `name`, `icon`, `device_class`, ...\n  * `device_info` — device grouping: `id`, `name`, `manufacturer`, ...\n  * `state` — initial state; also the reset-to-default target\n  * `inherit` — `true` to adopt the entity's current HA state on load (default `false`)\n\nInbound messages set the state from `payload` (a bare value, or a map with a\n`\"state\"`/`:state` key). A `payload` of `%{reset: true}` (or `{:reset, _}`)\nresets to the flow-declared `state`.\n\nUse `HomeElixir.Nodered.remove/2` to force-delete the entity.","ref":"HomeElixir.Nodes.Device.html"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.Nodes.Function","doc":"Applies a function to each message. Config is `fun: &Mod.fun/1` (a remote\nfunction). It receives the `HomeElixir.Msg` and returns a new `Msg` (or a raw\nvalue, wrapped as `payload`), or `nil` to drop the message.","ref":"HomeElixir.Nodes.Function.html"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.Nodes.Inject","doc":"Passthrough source node: re-emits each incoming message unchanged. Use it as\nthe entry point of a flow that starts from an external trigger (a web button\nvia the `ui:` config) rather than from an HA event.\n\nPair it with a `ui:` config so the web UI renders a control for it:\n\n    node(\"start\", HomeElixir.Nodes.Inject, ui: %{type: \"button\", label: \"Go\"})\n    wire(\"start\", \"next\")","ref":"HomeElixir.Nodes.Inject.html"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.Nodes.Logger","doc":"Logs each incoming message and produces no output. A debug/observation node\n(the Node-RED `debug` equivalent), useful as a flow endpoint and for e2e.","ref":"HomeElixir.Nodes.Logger.html"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.Nodes.Schedule","doc":"Source node: fires on wall-clock times given by a 5-field cron expression\n(e.g. `\"*/2 * * * *\"` every 2 minutes, `\"0 15 * * 1\"` Monday at 3pm).\n\nConfig:\n  * `cron`    — 5-field cron expression (required). Invalid cron is a load-time error.\n  * `payload` — term to emit (default `\"fire\"`).\n  * `topic`   — Msg topic (default `\"schedule\"`).\n\nNo input wires. Each fire emits a `Msg` and reschedules the next run.\nNext-run math is wall-clock / local time via `Crontab.Scheduler`.\n\nExample (auto-increment a counter every 2 minutes):\n    node(\"tick\", HomeElixir.Nodes.Schedule, cron: \"*/2 * * * *\", payload: \"inc\")","ref":"HomeElixir.Nodes.Schedule.html"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.Nodes.Service","doc":"Sink node: calls a Home Assistant service when a message arrives.\n\nConfig:\n * `domain` — e.g. `\"light\"` (required)\n * `service` — e.g. `\"turn_on\"` (required)\n * `data` — optional static `service_data` map; a map `payload` on the\n   incoming message is merged in (message wins)\n\nThe call is sent and its ack awaited, ensuring the service is reliably\ndelivered over the WebSocket (a fire-and-forget cast proved lossy).","ref":"HomeElixir.Nodes.Service.html"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.Nodes.Sink","doc":"Records every incoming message (most recent first). Useful as a flow endpoint\nand for tests; read it back via `HomeElixir.Registry.node_state/2`.","ref":"HomeElixir.Nodes.Sink.html"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.Nodes.StateChanged","doc":"Source node: emits a message when a Home Assistant entity's state changes.\n\nConfig:\n  * `entity_id` — optional; emit only for this entity. Omit for all entities.\n\nThe emitted message has `payload` = the new state, `topic` = the entity id,\nand `data` = `%{entity_id:, old_state:, new_state:}`.","ref":"HomeElixir.Nodes.StateChanged.html"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.HA","doc":"Access to the shared, named `HomeElixir.HA.Client`.\n\nHome Assistant uses a single WebSocket connection shared by every HA-aware\nnode (mirroring Node-RED). The app starts one named client when\n`HA_URL`/`HA_TOKEN` are configured; nodes reach it through this module.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.activate/1","doc":"Store `token` as the shared HA auth (beats the static config until the next\nlogin) and make sure the shared WS client runs with the current token\n(start it when absent, restart it when it holds a different one). Called on\na successful web login.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#activate/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.build_range/2","doc":"Resolve a history `range` to a `{start_iso, end_iso}` UTC pair. `nil` is the\nlast hour; a number is a look-back in hours; `{start, end}` is explicit\n(DateTime or ISO8601). `now` (unix seconds) is injectable for tests.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#build_range/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.client/0","doc":"The pid of the shared client, or `nil` if it is not running.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#client/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.client_name/0","doc":"The atom name of the shared client process.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#client_name/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.config_url/0","doc":"The configured HA endpoint (env `HA_URL` or config `:ha_url`), or `nil`.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#config_url/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.connected?/0","doc":"True when a shared client is running.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#connected?/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.device_entity_ids/2","doc":"The `entity_id`s belonging to `device_id`, from an entity-registry list.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#device_entity_ids/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.device_history/2","doc":"State history for every entity on `device_id` over `range` (see `history/2`).\nReturns `{:ok, [state_map]}` or `{:error, reason}`.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#device_history/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.device_states/1","doc":"The current states of every entity on `device_id` (resolved via the entity\nregistry), in registry order. Returns `{:ok, [state_map]}` or `{:error, reason}`.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#device_states/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.ensure_client/0","doc":"Ensure the shared WS client is running with the current token.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#ensure_client/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.filter_states/2","doc":"The states for `entity_ids` (in that order), from a `get_states` list.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#filter_states/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.find_state/2","doc":"Find one entity's state in a `get_states` list, or `nil`.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#find_state/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.flatten_history/1","doc":"Flatten HA's history response (a list of per-entity lists) to one list.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#flatten_history/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.history/2","doc":"State history for `ids` (an entity_id or a list of them) over `range`.\n`range` is `nil` (last hour), a number (look back N hours), or `{start, end}`\n(DateTime or ISO8601 strings). Returns `{:ok, [state_map]}` (a flat list) or\n`{:error, reason}`.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#history/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.rest_base/0","doc":"The HA REST base URL (`scheme://host[:port][/prefix]`) for HTTP API calls,\nderived from the configured endpoint (which may be a `wss://`/`ws://`\nWebSocket URL). Keeps any proxy path prefix: `ws://supervisor/core/api/websocket`\nbecomes `http://supervisor/core`, so callers append `/api/...` as usual.\n`nil` when no HA endpoint is configured.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#rest_base/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.rest_prefix/0","doc":"The REST path prefix implied by the configured endpoint (`\"/core\"` for the\nsupervisor Core proxy, `\"\"` for a direct Core URL), or `nil` when no endpoint\nis configured.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#rest_prefix/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.snapshot/1","doc":"Fetch a camera snapshot for `entity_id` as raw bytes, via HA's\n`/api/camera_proxy/{entity}` REST endpoint, over Mint (a core dependency, so\ncallers don't need to install `req`). Returns `{:ok, binary}` or\n`{:error, reason}`.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#snapshot/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.snapshot_b64/1","doc":"Fetch a camera snapshot for `entity_id` and return it base64-encoded (for\ninlining as a `data:image/jpeg;base64,...` URL). Built on `snapshot/1`.\nReturns `{:ok, base64}` or `{:error, reason}`.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#snapshot_b64/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.state/1","doc":"The current state of one entity (a `get_states` entry: `%{\"entity_id\",\n\"state\", \"attributes\", \"last_changed\", \"last_updated\"}`), or `{:error, reason}`.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#state/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.token/0","doc":"The HA auth token used for all HA API calls (the shared WS client and REST).\nFirst match wins:\n\n  1. env `SUPERVISOR_TOKEN` — present only when running as an HA add-on; the\n     only token the supervisor's Core proxy accepts\n  2. the token from the most recent web login (HA OAuth), stored in global\n     config\n  3. env `HA_TOKEN` (the NixOS module)\n  4. config `:ha_token` (e.g. config/secret.exs)\n\n`nil` when nothing is configured.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#token/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.web_base_url/0","doc":"The public web origin (config `:web_base_url`), or `nil`.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#web_base_url/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.whoami/1","doc":"Resolve who an HA access token belongs to via the WebSocket `auth/current_user`\ncommand, on a transient one-shot client. Returns `{:ok, {name, is_admin}}` or\n`{:error, reason}`.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.html#whoami/1"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.HA.Client","doc":"A client for the Home Assistant WebSocket API.\n\nMaintains a single authenticated WebSocket connection (through a transport,\ndefault `HomeElixir.HA.Transport.Mint`), and offers:\n\n  * `call/3` — id-correlated request/response\n  * `subscribe_events/3` — HA event fan-out to a process\n  * automatic reconnection (and re-auth + re-subscribe) after a drop\n\nA transport is a GenServer following a small convention: it is started with\n`module.start_link(owner: pid, url: url, token: token)`, sends\n`{:ha_transport, :connected}`, `{:ha_transport, :text, binary}` and\n`{:ha_transport, :closed, reason}` to its owner, and handles\n`GenServer.cast(transport, {:ha_send, json})` to send an outbound frame.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.Client.html"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.Client.call/4","doc":"Send a request and await its correlated result.\n\nReturns the `result` field on success (may be `nil`), or\n`{:error, %{code: code, message: message}}` when Home Assistant reports an\nerror. Returns `{:error, {:not_connected, status}}` if not yet connected.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.Client.html#call/4"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.Client.channels_for/2","doc":"The current `[{id, node_id}]` for every channel discovered by `to` (the `node_id`\nis read from each discovery frame).\n\nRe-derive this rather than trusting the `id` returned by `discover/3`: a\nreconnect's re-discovery reassigns a fresh id to each channel, so a cached\nid→thing map goes stale and inbound frames on the new ids are dropped.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.Client.html#channels_for/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.Client.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.Client.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.Client.discover/3","doc":"Register a message-id channel for a long-lived HA feature (e.g. a Node-RED\ndevice). A fresh id from the shared monotonically-increasing counter (the same\none `call/3` uses, so HA's \"ids must increase\" rule holds) is injected into\n`discovery_frame`'s `\"id\"`; frames arriving with that id are forwarded to `to`\nas `{:ha_channel, id, frame}`. The frame is sent now if connected and re-sent\non every (re)connect, so the entity re-establishes after a dropped connection.\nReturns the channel `id` (so the caller can route inbound channel frames).","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.Client.html#discover/3"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.Client.fire/3","doc":"Send a request and ignore its response (fire-and-forget).\n\nUse for `call_service` and similar, where the caller does not need HA's ack.\nReturns `:ok` (the request is dropped if not connected).","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.Client.html#fire/3"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.Client.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.Client.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.Client.status/1","doc":"Current connection status: `:connecting`, `:authenticating`, `:connected` or `:disconnected`.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.Client.html#status/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.Client.subscribe_events/4","doc":"Subscribe to Home Assistant events. Matching events are sent to `to` as\n`{:ha_event, ref, event}`. Returns the subscription `ref`.\n\nThe subscription is registered immediately; if not yet connected it is sent\nautomatically on (re)connect, so callers need not wait for a connection.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.Client.html#subscribe_events/4"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.Client.token/1","doc":"The access token this client authenticates with.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.Client.html#token/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.Client.transport_pid/1","doc":"The pid of the active transport (for diagnostics/tests); `nil` when down.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.Client.html#transport_pid/1"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.HA.LiveUpdate","doc":"Send and dismiss Android/iOS Home Assistant companion **Live Activities** to a\nperson's devices — the reusable core. Flows just call `update/3` / `dismiss/2`.\n\nA person's companion devices are discovered from their `person. ` entity's\n`device_trackers` list; each `device_tracker. ` maps to the notify service\n`mobile_app_ ` (the `notify` domain is added separately, so the service\nname carries no `notify.` prefix).\n\nThe companion reads its Live Activity fields (`tag`, `live_update`, `progress`,\n`progress_max`, `chronometer`, `when`, `notification_icon`, `color`, ...) from\nthe notify service's **`data`** dict; `title`/`message` stay top-level (HA's\nschema requires them there). `update/3` adds a fixed `tag` and\n`live_update: true` so a later call with the same tag updates the activity in\nplace; `dismiss/2` clears it by tag.\n\nThe dispatch is **fire-and-forget** (an async `cast` to the HA client), so a\ncaller never blocks waiting for delivery; only the single `get_states` read\nthat resolves a person's devices is a (bounded) blocking call. Android requires\nAndroid 16+ for Live Activities to render.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.LiveUpdate.html"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.LiveUpdate.dismiss/2","doc":"Dismiss the Live Activity `tag` on every companion device of `person`.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.LiveUpdate.html#dismiss/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.LiveUpdate.update/3","doc":"Send (or update) a Live Activity on every companion device of `person`.\n\n`person` is a person name (`\"mog\"`) or full entity (`\"person.mog\"`); `tag` keys\nthe activity; `payload` holds the companion fields (`title`, `message`,\n`progress`, `progress_max`, `chronometer`, `when`, `notification_icon`,\n`color`, ...). Returns `{:ok, count}` (devices dispatched to) or `{:error,\nreason}`: `:not_connected`, `:person_not_found`, `:no_devices`, or `:ha_timeout`.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.LiveUpdate.html#update/3"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.HA.OAuth","doc":"Home Assistant local OAuth (authorization code + PKCE).\n\nhome-elixir registers with HA as a local OAuth client whose `client_id` is its\nown origin (the `:web_base_url` config); HA issues no client secret for local\nclients. `start_login/0` begins a flow (minting the `state` + PKCE pair, kept\nin `HomeElixir.HA.PendingLogins`) and returns the HA authorize URL to redirect\nthe browser to; `complete_login/2` validates the redirected `state` and\nexchanges the `code` for an access token.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.OAuth.html"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.OAuth.complete_login/2","doc":"Exchange a `code` for an access token, validating `state`.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.OAuth.html#complete_login/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.OAuth.start_login/0","doc":"Begin a login; returns `{:ok, authorize_url, state}` or `{:error, reason}`.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.OAuth.html#start_login/0"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.HA.OAuthStrategy","doc":"The `OAuth2.Strategy.AuthCode` flow, minus the `Authorization: Basic` header.\n\noauth2 always sends `Basic base64(client_id:client_secret)`. For Home\nAssistant's local client the `client_id` is a URL, so that header decodes to a\ngarbage client id and the token exchange is rejected. HA identifies the client\nfrom `client_id` in the request body instead, so we omit the header.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.OAuthStrategy.html"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.HA.PendingLogins","doc":"Shared store for in-flight OAuth logins, keyed by the `state` value.\n\nA named GenServer so the mapping survives across Cowboy worker processes\n(each HTTP request runs in a short-lived worker; the state minted at\n`/oauth/start` must still be findable at `/oauth/callback`).\n\nEach entry is `{code_verifier, expiry_ms}` and is consumed exactly once\n(taken on read), so a captured redirect URL cannot be replayed.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.PendingLogins.html"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.PendingLogins.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.PendingLogins.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.PendingLogins.get/1","doc":"Non-destructively read the verifier for `state` (nil if absent/expired).","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.PendingLogins.html#get/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.PendingLogins.put/3","doc":"Store a pending `state` → `code_verifier`, valid for `ttl_ms`.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.PendingLogins.html#put/3"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.PendingLogins.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.PendingLogins.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.PendingLogins.take/1","doc":"Atomically fetch-and-delete the verifier for `state` (nil if absent/expired).","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.PendingLogins.html#take/1"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.HA.Transport.Mint","doc":"WebSocket transport backed by Mint + Mint.WebSocket.\n\nImplements the transport convention expected by `HomeElixir.HA.Client`:\nstarted with `start_link/1` (`owner:`, `url:`), reports\n`{:ha_transport, :connected | :text, binary | :closed, reason}` to its owner,\nand sends outbound frames given via `GenServer.cast(transport, {:ha_send, json})`.\n\nThe process owns an active-mode Mint connection, so inbound TCP/SSL data\narrives here as messages.\n\nValidated against a live Home Assistant over `wss://` (connect, auth, and a\n`get_states` round-trip). `mix run scripts/ha_validate.exs` reproduces it.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.Transport.Mint.html"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.Transport.Mint.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.Transport.Mint.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.HA.Transport.Mint.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.HA.Transport.Mint.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.NodeRedStatus","doc":"Tracks whether the Node-RED Companion integration is installed in Home\nAssistant. Probed once at startup (and re-checkable on demand from the admin\npage).\n\nStatus is three-state:\n\n  * `:loaded` — the integration is added & set up (its `nodered/version`\n    websocket command is registered, which only happens once a config entry\n    is loaded)\n  * `:absent` — HA is reachable but the integration is not added/set up\n  * `:unknown` — can't tell (no HA client, not connected yet, or a probe error)\n\nOnly `:absent` changes behavior (the flow→Node-RED sync stops and `device`\nnodes go inert). `:unknown` keeps existing behavior so a slow or absent HA\nconnection at boot never raises a false \"missing\" warning.","ref":"HomeElixir.NodeRedStatus.html"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.NodeRedStatus.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"HomeElixir.NodeRedStatus.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.NodeRedStatus.present?/0","doc":"True when the Node-RED integration is present.","ref":"HomeElixir.NodeRedStatus.html#present?/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.NodeRedStatus.recheck/0","doc":"Re-run the probe now and return the new status.","ref":"HomeElixir.NodeRedStatus.html#recheck/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.NodeRedStatus.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.NodeRedStatus.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.NodeRedStatus.status/0","doc":"Current status: `:loaded`, `:absent`, or `:unknown`.","ref":"HomeElixir.NodeRedStatus.html#status/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.NodeRedStatus.version/0","doc":"The detected integration version, when present (`nil` otherwise).","ref":"HomeElixir.NodeRedStatus.html#version/0"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.Nodered","doc":"Helpers for managing Node-RED-integration entities from Elixir.","ref":"HomeElixir.Nodered.html"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Nodered.remove/3","doc":"Force-remove a device previously presented via `HomeElixir.Nodes.Device`.\n\nSends a `nodered/discovery` frame with `remove: true`, deleting the entity\nfrom Home Assistant. Use after unloading a flow (or to clean up a leftover\ndevice) — unloading a flow leaves the entity in place (it goes unavailable\nwhen this service's connection drops).","ref":"HomeElixir.Nodered.html#remove/3"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.Auth","doc":"Local accounts (Mnesia), in-memory sessions (ETS), and PBKDF2 password\nhashing via OTP `:crypto` — no external deps, so the hermetic Nix build is\nuntouched.\n\nOn start it seeds accounts from `:home_elixir, :auth_users` (username =>\npassword) and always ensures an `admin`: its password from that config, or a\nfreshly generated one (printed to the log) when none is configured.\n\nA user logs in with a local password (`login/2`) or a Home Assistant token\n(`login_ha_token/1`), whose identity and role are resolved via HA's WebSocket\n`auth/current_user` (`is_admin` maps to the local `admin` role).","ref":"HomeElixir.Auth.html"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Auth.change_password/3","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Auth.html#change_password/3"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Auth.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"HomeElixir.Auth.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Auth.cookie_name/0","doc":"The session cookie name.","ref":"HomeElixir.Auth.html#cookie_name/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Auth.create_session/2","doc":"Create a session for a user; returns the opaque token to store in a cookie.","ref":"HomeElixir.Auth.html#create_session/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Auth.create_user/3","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Auth.html#create_user/3"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Auth.delete_session/1","doc":"Drop a session token (logout / user deletion).","ref":"HomeElixir.Auth.html#delete_session/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Auth.delete_user/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Auth.html#delete_user/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Auth.ensure_ha_user/1","doc":"Auto-authenticate a user from HA ingress (X-Remote-User-Name). Creates them if new.","ref":"HomeElixir.Auth.html#ensure_ha_user/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Auth.ha_identity/2","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Auth.html#ha_identity/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Auth.list_users/0","doc":"All users as [%{name, role}].","ref":"HomeElixir.Auth.html#list_users/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Auth.login/2","doc":"Verify a local username/password; returns `{:ok, {username, role}}`.","ref":"HomeElixir.Auth.html#login/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Auth.login_ha_token/1","doc":"Validate an HA token: resolves its identity via HA's WebSocket\n`auth/current_user` and maps `is_admin` to the local `admin` role.","ref":"HomeElixir.Auth.html#login_ha_token/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Auth.reset_password/2","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Auth.html#reset_password/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Auth.resolve_session/1","doc":"Resolve a session token to `{user_id, role}` or `{:error, :unauthorized}`.","ref":"HomeElixir.Auth.html#resolve_session/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Auth.set_role/2","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Auth.html#set_role/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Auth.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Auth.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Auth.user_from_conn/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Auth.html#user_from_conn/1"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.AuthGuard","doc":"Wraps `HomeElixir.Web` and enforces a session on every route except the public\nones (`/login`, `/api/login`, static assets, favicon). On success it assigns\n`conn.assigns.user = {username, role}` and hands the conn to `HomeElixir.Web`;\non failure it redirects HTML requests to `/login` and answers `/api/*` with 401.","ref":"HomeElixir.AuthGuard.html"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.AuthGuard.call/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Plug.call/2 .","ref":"HomeElixir.AuthGuard.html#call/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.AuthGuard.init/1","doc":"Callback implementation for  Plug.init/1 .","ref":"HomeElixir.AuthGuard.html#init/1"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.EntityBrowser","doc":"Build an Area > Device > Entity tree of Home Assistant entities, for the\neditor's entity browser. `build/3` is pure and assembles the tree from three\nread-only HA lists; `tree/0` fetches them from the shared HA client.\n\nAreas come from each device's `area_id` (there is no reliable \"list areas\"\ncommand across HA versions), so area labels are the prettified area slug.","ref":"HomeElixir.EntityBrowser.html"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.EntityBrowser.build/3","doc":"Pure: build the Area > Device > Entity tree from three HA lists.\n\n`states` (`get_states`), `registry` (`config/entity_registry/list`),\n`devices` (`config/device_registry/list`). An entity's area is its own\n`area_id`, else its device's; with no area it goes under `\"No area\"`. Entities\nwith no device are listed loose under their area; a `device_id` not in\n`devices` is named `\"Unnamed device\"`. Returns a list of\n`%{\"name\", \"devices\" => [%{\"name\", \"entities\"}], \"entities\"}` maps, each\nentity a `%{\"id\", \"name\", \"state\", \"unit\", \"cls\"}` map.","ref":"HomeElixir.EntityBrowser.html#build/3"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.EntityBrowser.tree/0","doc":"Fetch and build the tree. `connected: false` when no HA client is running.","ref":"HomeElixir.EntityBrowser.html#tree/0"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.Examples","doc":"Bundled example flows, kept in a separate read-only `examples/` dir (outside the\nuser's `flows/` dir). They can be listed, viewed, and copied into the user's\nflows (verbatim) so they can be edited. They are never loaded or run in place.","ref":"HomeElixir.Examples.html"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Examples.copy/1","doc":"Copy an example flow, verbatim, into the user's flows dir under the same base\nname. Returns `{:ok, name}`, or `{:error, :exists}` / `{:error, :not_found}`.","ref":"HomeElixir.Examples.html#copy/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Examples.list/0","doc":"All example flows as `%{name, path}`, sorted by name.","ref":"HomeElixir.Examples.html#list/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Examples.source/1","doc":"The source of one example flow, or `{:error, :not_found}`.","ref":"HomeElixir.Examples.html#source/1"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.Log","doc":"In-memory ring buffer of recent log lines, fed by `HomeElixir.LogHandler`.\n\nThe web log page polls `lines/1` for entries newer than a given id, so the\npage grows as the app logs.","ref":"HomeElixir.Log.html"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Log.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"HomeElixir.Log.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Log.init/1","doc":"Callback implementation for  GenServer.init/1 .","ref":"HomeElixir.Log.html#init/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Log.lines/1","doc":"Return `[id, line]` entries with `id > since` (newest last).","ref":"HomeElixir.Log.html#lines/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Log.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Log.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.Terminal","doc":"Cowboy WebSocket handler that gives the browser a real IEx bridged over\nxterm.js.\n\nWhen the app itself is a named Erlang node (started with `--sname\nhome_elixir`, see README) the shell is `iex --remsh home_elixir` — a genuine\nremote connection into this app's VM, with its code path, so `Node.list()`,\n`HomeElixir.FlowStore.list()`, the HA client, etc. all see the live instance\n rather than a second app. `script` runs IEx in a pseudo-terminal so keystrokes\n echo and line editing work over the port.\n\nIf the app is NOT a named node, it falls back to a self-contained\n`iex -S mix` (its own app instance) with `HOME_ELIXIR_NO_WEB=1` so it stays\noff the parent's web port.","ref":"HomeElixir.Terminal.html"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Terminal.init/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  :cowboy_websocket.init/2 .","ref":"HomeElixir.Terminal.html#init/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Terminal.terminate/3","doc":"Callback implementation for  :cowboy_websocket.terminate/3 .","ref":"HomeElixir.Terminal.html#terminate/3"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Terminal.websocket_handle/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  :cowboy_websocket.websocket_handle/2 .","ref":"HomeElixir.Terminal.html#websocket_handle/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Terminal.websocket_info/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  :cowboy_websocket.websocket_info/2 .","ref":"HomeElixir.Terminal.html#websocket_info/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Terminal.websocket_init/1","doc":"Callback implementation for  :cowboy_websocket.websocket_init/1 .","ref":"HomeElixir.Terminal.html#websocket_init/1"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.Web","doc":"Web UI + JSON API for managing flows: a list page, an inline-highlighted\neditor for flow files, and a live-updating log page.\n\nThe `/terminal` route gives the browser a real IEx attached to the running\napp: when the app is a named node it opens `iex --remsh home_elixir` (a\ndistributed connection into this VM), otherwise it falls back to `iex -S mix`.\n\nRoutes:\n  GET  /                        flow list (load/unload/edit)\n  GET  /edit                    editor for a new flow\n  GET  /edit/:name              editor preloaded with flows/:name.ex\n  GET  /logs                    live log view\n  GET  /terminal                real IEx in the browser (xterm.js over WebSocket)\n  GET  /api/flows               list flows (JSON)\n  GET  /api/entity_tree         HA Area > Device > Entity tree (JSON)\n  GET  /api/logs?since=N        log lines newer than N (JSON)\n  GET  /api/flows/:name/ui      UI elements for one flow (JSON)\n  POST /api/flows/:name/load | unload | reload\n  POST /api/flows/reload        reload all loaded flows\n  POST /api/flows/save | check   (save reuses the editor's path via the X-Flow-Name header; new files derive it from the module)","ref":"HomeElixir.Web.html"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Web.base_path/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Web.html#base_path/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Web.call/2","doc":"Callback implementation for  Plug.call/2 .","ref":"HomeElixir.Web.html#call/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Web.dispatch/2","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Web.html#dispatch/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Web.home_path/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Web.html#home_path/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Web.ingress?/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Web.html#ingress?/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Web.init/1","doc":"Callback implementation for  Plug.init/1 .","ref":"HomeElixir.Web.html#init/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Web.login_path/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Web.html#login_path/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Web.name_from_source/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Web.html#name_from_source/1"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.Config","doc":"Layered, editable configuration for flows.\n\nResolution order (first hit wins):\n\n  1. flow-specific value — set in the UI, or seeded by the flow's `setup/0`\n  2. global value — shared across all flows\n  3. `Application.get_env(:home_elixir, key)` — config/*.exs (e.g. secret.exs)\n  4. `System.get_env(\"KEY\")` — an environment variable\n  5. the supplied default\n\nRead it from inside a flow — the current flow is the ambient context set by\nthe node engine and `setup/0`, so no flow argument is needed:\n\n    HomeElixir.Config.get(:llm_url, \"http://localhost:42808/v1\")\n\nFlows declare their editable keys (and defaults) in `setup/0` so they appear\nin the UI and can be overridden without editing code:\n\n    def setup do\n      HomeElixir.Config.seed(%{llm_url: \"http://localhost:42808/v1\"})\n      HomeElixir.Config.seed(%{llm_api_key: \"sk-...\"}, scope: :global)\n    end\n\n`seed/2` is only-if-absent, so a value a user later edits in the UI survives\nflow reloads and restarts. Backed by Mnesia (started by `HomeElixir.Application`\nbefore any flow loads).","ref":"HomeElixir.Config.html"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Config.delete/2","doc":"Remove a value for a scope — subsequent reads fall back to the next layer.","ref":"HomeElixir.Config.html#delete/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Config.flow_config/1","doc":"All flow-specific config for a flow (name => %{key => value}).","ref":"HomeElixir.Config.html#flow_config/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Config.get/2","doc":"Resolve a config value per the layered order. Returns the value.","ref":"HomeElixir.Config.html#get/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Config.global_config/0","doc":"All global config (%{key => value}).","ref":"HomeElixir.Config.html#global_config/0"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Config.put/3","doc":"Set a value for a scope — a flow name or `:global`.","ref":"HomeElixir.Config.html#put/3"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Config.put_flow/2","doc":"Set a flow-specific value for the current (ambient) flow.","ref":"HomeElixir.Config.html#put_flow/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Config.put_global/2","doc":"Set a global value (shared across all flows).","ref":"HomeElixir.Config.html#put_global/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Config.resolve/2","doc":"Resolve a config value, returning `{value, source}` where source is one of\n`:flow`, `:global`, `:app`, `:system`, or `:default`. Used by the UI to badge\nwhere each value comes from.","ref":"HomeElixir.Config.html#resolve/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Config.secret?/1","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Config.html#secret?/1"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Config.seed/2","doc":"Declare editable keys + defaults for the current flow. `scope:` defaults to\n`:flow` (per-flow); pass `scope: :global` for values shared across flows.\nOnly-if-absent across the whole resolution chain, so it never shadows a value\nalready set at any layer (flow/global/app/system) — a user's edit or app\nconfig always wins over a re-seed.","ref":"HomeElixir.Config.html#seed/2"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Config.start/0","doc":"","ref":"HomeElixir.Config.html#start/0"},{"type":"module","title":"HomeElixir.Dep","doc":"Install external Hex dependencies at runtime, Livebook-style, without editing\n`mix.exs`.\n\n`install/1` builds the given deps in an isolated throwaway Mix project under\nthe user cache — as a `mix` subprocess, since `Mix.install/1` refuses to run\ninside an active Mix project — and adds the resulting code paths to the\nrunning VM. Flows call this from their `setup/0`.\n\nThe build is cached in `~/.cache/home_elixir/deps`, so only the first install\nof a dep hits the network; later loads and restarts reuse it. Because the\nproject is shared, `install/1` accumulates the union of all deps ever\nrequested, so   one flow's install never evicts another flow's compiled beams.\n\nAt boot, `reset_if_stale/0` wipes the compiled cache only when the set of\ndeps declared across the flow files changed since last boot — so a changed\nset rebuilds clean, while an unchanged set reuses the warm cache.","ref":"HomeElixir.Dep.html"},{"type":"function","title":"HomeElixir.Dep.install/1","doc":"Fetch, compile, and load `deps` (a keyword list, e.g. `[{:timex, \"~> 3.7\"}]`).","ref":"HomeElixir.Dep.html#install/1"},{"type":"extras","title":"HomeElixir","doc":"# HomeElixir\n\nA Node-RED-style flow engine for Home Assistant in Elixir. Flows are plain `.ex`\nfiles in `flows/`; the app connects to Home Assistant over its WebSocket API and\nruns the flows as an OTP supervision tree.\n\n[![Open your Home Assistant instance and show the add add-ons and integrations page to install the add-on.](https://my.home-assistant.io/badges/supervisor_addon.svg)](https://my.home-assistant.io/redirect/supervisor_addon/?addon=88eff496_home-elixir&repository_url=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fmogorman%2Fhome_elixir)\n\n> **Live notifications:** Live Activities work on iOS and Android, but the Android\n> companion app currently has broken live-notification *icon* support — the icon\n> does not render (a workaround exists, see\n> [home-assistant/android#5758](https://github.com/home-assistant/android/issues/5758#issuecomment-3297763341)).\n> See the `liveupdate` example.","ref":"readme.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Running - HomeElixir","doc":"Start the app and its web UI (flow list, editor, live logs):\n\n```sh\nHA_URL=wss://... HA_TOKEN=... mix run --no-halt\n# then open http://localhost:4000\n```\n\n`HA_URL`/`HA_TOKEN` are optional — without them, flows that don't need HA still run.\n\nStart it as a **named node** too, so a dev shell can attach to the running app\n(see Dev shell):\n\n```sh\nERL_AFLAGS=\"-sname home_elixir -setcookie home_elixir\" \\\n  HA_URL=wss://... HA_TOKEN=... mix run --no-halt\n```","ref":"readme.html#running"},{"type":"extras","title":"Dev shell - HomeElixir","doc":"The dev shell is real IEx **attached to the running app** — a distributed\nconnection into the app's VM, not a second app instance. This works when the\nserver is started as the named node `:home_elixir` (command above).\n\n**In the browser** — open the **IEx** link in the web UI (or `/terminal`). It\nopens a genuine `iex --remsh home_elixir` over xterm.js/WebSocket, so\n`HomeElixir.FlowStore.list()`, the HA client, etc. all see the live instance.\n\n**In a terminal:**\n\n```sh\nERL_AFLAGS=\"-sname home_elixir_dev -setcookie home_elixir\" iex --remsh home_elixir\n```\n\nThe usual IEx helpers work. `HomeElixir.FlowStore.*` calls are node-aware, so\nthey reach the running app's server from the attached shell. If the server is\nnot a named node, the browser tab falls back to a self-contained `iex -S mix`.","ref":"readme.html#dev-shell"},{"type":"extras","title":"Web UI - HomeElixir","doc":"- `/` — flow list (load / unload / reload)\n- `/edit` — create or edit a flow (highlighted editor with a live compile check)\n- `/controls` — buttons / state widgets declared by loaded flows\n- `/logs` — live app log\n- `/terminal` — in-browser IEx attached to the running app","ref":"readme.html#web-ui"},{"type":"extras","title":"Flows - HomeElixir","doc":"Each file in `flows/` is one flow module (`use HomeElixir.Flow`, `node/3`,\n`wire/2`). Create/edit them in the web editor, or drop a `.ex` file into\n`flows/` and load it from the list page. The set of loaded flows is persisted\n(in the Mnesia flow-state DB) and restored on start.\n\nSubfolders group flows in the list (e.g. `flows/living_room/counter.ex` shows\nunder a collapsible `living_room` folder, matching a\n`HomeElixir.Flows.LivingRoom.Counter` module).","ref":"readme.html#flows"},{"type":"extras","title":"Writing a flow - HomeElixir","doc":"Nodes are declared with `node(id, module, config)` and connected with\n`wire(from, to)`; several sources can share a target with\n`wire([\"a\", \"b\"], \"c\")`. In handler flows, `Inject` nodes with no outgoing\nwire are connected to `handle/1`, and state-badge nodes (`ui: %{type: \"state\"}`)\nwith no input are fed by its output — both explicit wires override. A handler\nreturns a value to wake its output nodes (state-changing clauses return the\nFlowState op's result); unmatched input returns nil and is dropped. A\n`HomeElixir.Msg` flows from a source node along the wires; a node's output 0 is\nforwarded to the next node(s).\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule HomeElixir.Flows.Kitchen do\n  use HomeElixir.Flow\n\n  # An optional local transform, referenced by the Function node below.\n  def shout(m), do: %{m | payload: m.payload |> to_string() |> String.upcase()}\n\n  node(\"in\",  HomeElixir.Nodes.Inject,   ui: %{type: \"button\", label: \"Go\"})\n  node(\"cap\", HomeElixir.Nodes.Function, fun: &__MODULE__.shout/1)\n  node(\"out\", HomeElixir.Nodes.Logger)\n  wire(\"in\", \"cap\")\n  wire(\"cap\", \"out\")\nend\n```","ref":"readme.html#writing-a-flow"},{"type":"extras","title":"Using an external library (Livebook-style) - HomeElixir","doc":"A flow may define `setup/0`; it runs once when the flow is loaded, before any\nnode starts. Use `HomeElixir.Dep.install/1` inside it to pull a Hex dependency\nonto the code path at runtime — no `mix.exs` edit:\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule HomeElixir.Flows.NowClock do\n  use HomeElixir.Flow\n\n  def setup, do: HomeElixir.Dep.install([{:timex, \"~> 3.7\"}])\n\n  def now(m), do: %{m | payload: Timex.now() |> Timex.format!(\"{h12}:{m} {am}\")}\n\n  node(\"trigger\", HomeElixir.Nodes.Inject,\n       ui: %{type: \"button\", label: \"What time is it?\"})\n  node(\"clock\", HomeElixir.Nodes.Function, fun: &__MODULE__.now/1)\n  node(\"log\", HomeElixir.Nodes.Logger)\n  wire(\"trigger\", \"clock\")\n  wire(\"clock\", \"log\")\nend\n```\n\nThe build is cached in `~/.cache/home_elixir/deps`, so only the first load of a\ndep set hits the network.","ref":"readme.html#using-an-external-library-livebook-style"},{"type":"extras","title":"Handler flows - HomeElixir","doc":"For a flow that just reacts to Home Assistant state changes, define `handle/1`\ninstead of wiring nodes. The Flow macro auto-wires an HA `state_changed` source\nto it and discards the return value — so a handler just matches the input it\ncares about and does work. The catch-all clause is added for you, so write only\nthe clauses you need:\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule HomeElixir.Flows.DoorWatch do\n  use HomeElixir.Flow\n\n  def handle(%{topic: \"sensor.front_door\", payload: \"open\"}) do\n    # do work (fire a service, log, send a message, ...)\n  end\nend\n```\n\nThe `topic` is the entity id and the `payload` is the new state; match on them\n(or use guards / `=~`) to pick the changes you care about.","ref":"readme.html#handler-flows"},{"type":"extras","title":"Nodes - HomeElixir","doc":"Built-in nodes live in `HomeElixir.Nodes`. A node is a module implementing\n`HomeElixir.Node` (`handle/2`, optional `init/1` and `trigger/2`).\n\n| Node | Role | Key config |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| `Inject` | Passthrough source; entry point for web-triggered flows | `ui` (button / state) |\n| `Function` | Apply an Elixir function to each message | `fun: &Mod.fun/1` |\n| `Sink` | Record messages (test / debug endpoint) | — |\n| `Logger` | Log each message to the app log | — |\n| `Service` | Call a Home Assistant service | `domain`, `service`, `data` |\n| `StateChanged` | Emit on HA state changes | `entity_id` (optional) |\n| `Device` | Present / own an HA entity via the Node-RED integration | `server_id`, `node_id`, `component`, `config`, `device_info`, `state` |\n\n**Web controls:** add `ui: %{type: \"button\", label: \"…\"}` (or `type: \"state\"`)\nto a node's config and it appears on `/controls`. Clicking a button sends a\nmessage into that node.","ref":"readme.html#nodes"},{"type":"extras","title":"API - HomeElixir","doc":"The app runs as an OTP application; these are the main entry points (all also\nreachable from the web UI or the dev shell).\n\n### `HomeElixir.FlowStore` — flow lifecycle\n\n| Function | Description |\n|----------|-------------|\n| `list/0` | All flow files with their loaded state |\n| `load(name)` / `unload(name)` | Start / stop a flow |\n| `reload(name)` / `reload_all/0` | Recompile + restart from disk |\n| `loaded?(name)` | Whether a flow is loaded |\n| `click(name, node, payload)` | Send a message into a node (web controls) |\n| `ui/0` / `flow_ui(name)` | UI elements, live-valued when loaded |\n| `check(source)` | Compile-check a source string without loading |\n| `forget(name)` | Drop the cached module atom (force recompile) |\n| `restore/0` | Reload the persisted set (Mnesia flow-state DB) |\n\n### `HomeElixir.Registry` — the supervised node tree\n\n| Function | Description |\n|----------|-------------|\n| `load(module)` / `unload(module)` | Start / stop a flow module's nodes |\n| `list/0` / `loaded?(module)` | Currently loaded flows |\n| `send_msg(module, node, msg)` | Cast a message into a node |\n| `node_state(module, node)` | Read a node's internal state (debug) |\n| `ui_elements/0` | UI elements declared by loaded flows |","ref":"readme.html#api"},{"type":"extras","title":"Other - HomeElixir","doc":"| Function | Description |\n|----------|-------------|\n| `HomeElixir.Msg.new(payload, opts)` | Build a message (`%{payload, topic, data, msgid}`) |\n| `HomeElixir.Dep.install(deps)` | Install Hex deps at runtime (Livebook-style) |\n| `HomeElixir.HA.client/0` / `connected?/0` | The shared HA WebSocket client |\n| `HomeElixir.HA.Client.call(client, type, payload)` | Correlated HA request |\n| `HomeElixir.HA.Client.fire(client, type, payload)` | Fire-and-forget HA request |\n| `HomeElixir.HA.Client.subscribe_events(client, type, to)` | Subscribe to HA events |\n| `HomeElixir.Nodered.remove(server_id, node_id)` | Force-delete a Node-RED device |","ref":"readme.html#other"},{"type":"extras","title":"Development - HomeElixir","doc":"Developed with the help of Qwen 3.8.","ref":"readme.html#development"}],"proglang":"elixir","content_type":"text/markdown","producer":{"name":"ex_doc","version":"0.40.4"}}